  "id": "COMPOUND:34725 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "Agallochin F is implicated in the biological activity of U373 MG through multiple indirect pathways. The drug targets SF-188, which is a target of both 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and Bungeiside A. These compounds, in turn, have targets that ultimately interact with U373 MG. This suggests a network of molecular interactions where Agallochin F influences the biological response of U373 MG through the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Agallochin F modulates the activity of upstream molecules, which then exert their effects on U373 MG. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the role of intermediate targets in mediating the drug's impact on the cell line.",
